  "caveats": [
    "All dimensions are teaching values; no claim of manufacturer or board-fabricator approval.",
    "The three PXML texts are prepared but have not been imported or run by this agent.",
    "PXML width/height expected to map X/Y for the slot; the XML table did not explicitly document axis mapping. Root must confirm drillSizeWidth=2.000 and drillSizeHeight=1.000 after import/export; adjust from evidence if they differ.",
    "PTH circular THERMAL_PAD values reproduce the official self-contained example style; they do not define a four-spoke flash. Negative-plane manufacturing artwork is out of scope and may report missing thermal flash.",
    "Slot thermal entries are intentionally absent; a production negative-plane slot thermal requires a verified matching flash or another validated connection strategy.",
    "NPTH NULL regular is intentional and only for the mechanical non-plated hole; do not copy it into the PTH inner-layer regular copper definition.",
    "NPTH anti/keepout data can make axlPadOnLayer return true despite no positive regular copper; inspect REGULAR figure and polygon count separately.",
    "No paste-mask definitions are emitted. Readback may expose missing layers as NULL pad objects; accept no non-NULL paste geometry and zero paste polygons.",
    "Mask dimensions are engineering teaching choices, not inferred from drill geometry or claimed datasheet specifications.",
    "Check importer log and reopened geometry and plating independently; on failure a pre-existing .pad could remain unchanged."
  ]
}
